{"name":"Bean Counter","hex":"#68755d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bean counter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is excessively interested in controlling or reducing expenses, increasing profits, or in quantitative details in general."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bean_counter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Below Deck Sailing Yacht","blocks":[{"text":"Below Deck Sailing Yacht is an American reality television series that was developed as the second spin-off of Below Deck. It premiered on Bravo on February 3, 2020."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/47/Below_Deck_Sailing_Yacht_Logo.png/330px-Below_Deck_Sailing_Yacht_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Below_Deck_Sailing_Yacht"},{"title":"Accountant","blocks":[{"text":"An accountant is a practitioner of accounting or accountancy.\nAccountants who have demonstrated competency through their professional associations' certification exams are certified to use titles such as Chartered Accountant, Chartered Certified Accountant or Certified Public Accountant, or Registered Public Accountant. Such professionals are granted certain responsibilities by statute, such as the ability to certify an organization's financial statements, and may be held liable for professional misconduct. Non-qualified accountants may be employed by a qualified accountant, or may work independently without statutory privileges and obligations."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accountant"},{"title":"Bean","blocks":[{"text":"A bean is the seed of plants in many genera of the legume family (Fabaceae) used as a vegetable for human consumption or animal feed. The seeds are sold fresh or preserved through drying (a pulse). Beans have been cultivated since the seventh millennium BCE in Thailand, and since the second millennium BCE in Europe and in Peru. Most beans, with the exception of peas, are summer crops. As legumes, the plants fix nitrogen and form seeds with a high protein content. They are produced on a scale of millions of tons annually in many countries, with India as the largest producer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/French_beans_J1.JPG/330px-French_beans_J1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bean"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Ledger.png/500px-Ledger.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Ledger.png/1280px-Ledger.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Ledger.png/500px-Ledger.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALedger.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/%D7%A4%D7%A0%D7%99_%D7%9B%D7%94%D7%9F_%D7%9E%D7%A0%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%97%D7%A9%D7%91%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%AA_%D7%AA%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%95%D7%9F_%D7%A8%D7%95%D7%98%D7%91%D7%A8%D7%92.jpg/500px-%D7%A4%D7%A0%D7%99_%D7%9B%D7%94%D7%9F_%D7%9E%D7%A0%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%97%D7%A9%D7%91%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%AA_%D7%AA%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%95%D7%9F_%D7%A8%D7%95%D7%98%D7%91%D7%A8%D7%92.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/%D7%A4%D7%A0%D7%99_%D7%9B%D7%94%D7%9F_%D7%9E%D7%A0%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%97%D7%A9%D7%91%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%AA_%D7%AA%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%95%D7%9F_%D7%A8%D7%95%D7%98%D7%91%D7%A8%D7%92.jpg/1280px-%D7%A4%D7%A0%D7%99_%D7%9B%D7%94%D7%9F_%D7%9E%D7%A0%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%97%D7%A9%D7%91%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%AA_%D7%AA%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%95%D7%9F_%D7%A8%D7%95%D7%98%D7%91%D7%A8%D7%92.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org